<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine wheat harvest 84.9 pct complete - gov't.</title>
<headline>Argentine wheat harvest 84.9 pct complete - gov't.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had harvested 84.9 percent of their 1996/97 wheat crop by January 3, the government's Agriculture Secretariat said in its weekly crop report Thursday.</p>
<p>But a shortage of combine harvesters and trucks in key Buenos Aires province could delay fieldwork, causing a loss in yield and quality. Maize sowing reached 94.9 percent. Recent rains have greatly helped maize. Soybean sowing reached 94.0 percent of intentions, helped by recent rain. Sunflower sowing was 98.1 percent over. Some 60,000 hectares of cotton have had to be resown in Chaco province following rain damage.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,983  100.0(100.0)  5,6409   84.9  (86.0)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,765   94.9 (94.1)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,383   94.0 (91.5)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,002   98.1 (99.5)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     760   95.2 (93.9)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	960   89.4  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655))</p>
